win32u: Create a per-monitor aware thread's child windows at the coordinates asked for.

What he saw: nothing yet on his desk; found while checking FL Studio's 96-dpi children (the dpi team agent,
2026-11-04). On a desk with a 175% primary and a 200% screen beside it, a per-monitor aware program's child window
came out the wrong size: a control asked at (20,20) 300x100 in a window on the 200% screen was created at (23,23)
343x114, and a child asked past the right edge of a window on the primary was shrunk to 7/8.

Mechanism: NtUserCreateWindowEx maps CREATESTRUCT through map_dpi_create_struct. A per-monitor aware thread has
get_thread_dpi() == 0, so it picks the dpi to map FROM with monitor_dpi_from_rect on cs.x/y/cx/cy. For a child those
are relative to the parent's client area, not screen coordinates, so the lookup lands on whichever monitor those
numbers happen to fall on, and the rect is scaled by that monitor's dpi over the child's (its top-level's). Upstream
Wine 11.10 does the same. SetWindowPos/MoveWindow from the same thread already treat its coordinates as the child's
own dpi (map_dpi_rect with 0 is the identity).

Windows behavior: a per-monitor aware thread speaks the dpi of the windows it creates; a child is created at the
client coordinates given (INFERRED; Windows probe dpichild.exe is waiting, it needs two monitors at different
scales and prints NOT DECISIVE otherwise).

Change: skip the mapping for a child (parent is not the desktop) when the thread is per-monitor aware and the new
window is monitor aware. Top-levels, DPI-unaware and system-aware threads are unchanged.

Not covered: a per-monitor thread creating a child of a window of another awareness (mixed hosting) keeps the old
mapping.

Lab evidence (desk-g: Virtual-0 175% primary, Virtual-1 200% to its right; probe dpichild.exe in a Prg1 copy):
fixed build 11.10-181d 7 of 8 runs created both children as asked (one run printed nothing before its first flush,
cause not found, not repeated in 4 timed runs with unbuffered output); same build with NEUTRON_CHILD_CREATE_DPI=0
2 of 2 mis-scaled exactly as stock 11.10-181 (3 of 3). FL Studio 2026 on 181 vs 181d: same 68 windows, same rects,
captures differ only in live text (hint bar, memory meter).

Kill switch: NEUTRON_CHILD_CREATE_DPI=0.


--- a/dlls/win32u/window.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/window.c
@@ -7094,6 +7094,19 @@
     return on;
 }
 
+/* NEUTRON child-create-dpi; kill switch NEUTRON_CHILD_CREATE_DPI=0 (see NtUserCreateWindowEx). */
+static BOOL neutron_child_create_dpi(void)
+{
+    static int on = -1;
+    if (on < 0)
+    {
+        const char *e = getenv( "NEUTRON_CHILD_CREATE_DPI" );
+        on = !e || e[0] != '0';
+        if (!on) ERR( "neutron-gateresolved: NEUTRON_CHILD_CREATE_DPI = 0 (environment)\n" );
+    }
+    return on;
+}
+
 /***********************************************************************
  *           map_dpi_create_struct
  */
@@ -7306,7 +7319,14 @@
         UINT raw_dpi;
         win_dpi = monitor_dpi_from_rect( rect, get_thread_dpi(), &raw_dpi );
     }
-    if (parent) map_dpi_create_struct( &cs, win_dpi );
+    /* NEUTRON child-create-dpi: a child's x/y/cx/cy are relative to its parent's client area, but with a per-monitor
+     * aware thread (get_thread_dpi() == 0) map_dpi_create_struct looked them up as SCREEN coordinates to pick the dpi
+     * to map from. A child of a window on a 200% screen, asked at (20,20) 300x100, came out (23,23) 343x114 beside a
+     * 175% primary; one asked past the primary's right edge was shrunk 7/8. A per-monitor aware thread already speaks
+     * the child's dpi (its top-level's), as SetWindowPos and MoveWindow assume: Windows creates it as asked. */
+    if (parent && (parent == get_desktop_window() || get_thread_dpi() || !neutron_child_create_dpi() ||
+                   !NTUSER_DPI_CONTEXT_IS_MONITOR_AWARE( get_window_dpi_awareness_context( hwnd ) )))
+        map_dpi_create_struct( &cs, win_dpi );
 
     context = set_thread_dpi_awareness_context( get_window_dpi_awareness_context( hwnd ));
 
